        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "6c7ca43740f5601c530f77d1b2cd6056989b3cc1",
            "parents": [
                "63ea9e3a3c6c027eb4f78ed8730715044de26a2e"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/61/85461/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Freddie Jheng",
                "email": "Freddie.Jheng@quantatw.com",
                "username": "FreddieJheng-quanta"
            },
            "createdOn": 1763713365,
            "author": {
                "name": "Freddie Jheng",
                "email": "Freddie.Jheng@quantatw.com",
                "username": "FreddieJheng-quanta"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/SensorPaths.cpp",
                    "line": 63,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Please just do constexpr std::array for this.\n\nconstructing a static map consumes memory for the life of the program, that we'd rather just stay RODATA"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/SensorPaths.cpp",
                    "line": 63,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Freddie Jheng",
                        "email": "Freddie.Jheng@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "FreddieJheng-quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Got it. Fixed"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/SensorPaths.cpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Could you please look at making this data structure constexpr global and applied to all uses so we don't have two structures that are the inverse of one another?\n\nstruct UnitMap{\n   std::string_view dbusPathName;\n   std::string_view dbusUnitName;\n   std::string_view emUnitName;\n};\n\nconstexpr std::array<UnitMap, N> = {{\n{\n\"xyz.openbmc_project.Sensor.Value.Unit.DegreesC\", \"DegreesC\", \"temperature\"\n\n}\n\n\nIf that's not possible, that's fine, but when we add new units, I'd like it to be very obvious that it needs added in several places.  Keeping them all in one table \"enforces\" that at a type level."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/SensorPaths.cpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Freddie Jheng",
                        "email": "Freddie.Jheng@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "FreddieJheng-quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Agreed. Created `UNITS_MAP` structure with all unit information:\n\n```cpp\nstruct UnitMap {\n    std::string_view dbusPathName;    // full D-Bus path\n    std::string_view dbusUnitName;    // short format from config\n    std::string_view emUnitName;      // path component\n};\n```\n\nNow both `getPathForUnits()` and `convertToFullUnits()` query from `UNITS_MAP`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/external/ExternalSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This is not the fault of this patch, but we should fix it.  This exception is not caught anywhere, so any bad config will result in a crash.  Please catch this exception in the level above."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/external/ExternalSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Freddie Jheng",
                        "email": "Freddie.Jheng@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "FreddieJheng-quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Fixed. Added validation and exception throwing in ExternalSensor.cpp:\n\n```cpp\nstd::string fullUnits = sensor_paths::convertToFullUnits(sensorUnits);\nif (fullUnits.empty())\n{\n    lg2::error(\"Invalid units for sensor: {UNITS}\", \"UNITS\", sensorUnits);\n    throw std::invalid_argument(\"Invalid units for sensor\");\n}\nsetInitialProperties(fullUnits);\n```\n\nAnd added exception handling in ExternalSensorMain.cpp's `createSensors()` function:\n\n```cpp\ntry\n{\n    sensorEntry = std::make_shared<ExternalSensor>(\n        sensorType, objectServer, dbusConnection, sensorName,\n        sensorUnits, std::move(sensorThresholds), interfacePath,\n        maxValue, minValue, timeoutSecs, readState);\n    sensorEntry->initWriteHook(\n        [&sensors, &reaperTimer](\n            const std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point& now) {\n            updateReaper(sensors, reaperTimer, now);\n        });\n\n    lg2::debug(\"ExternalSensor '{NAME}' created\", \"NAME\", sensorName);\n}\ncatch (const std::exception& e)\n{\n    lg2::error(\"Failed to create ExternalSensor '{NAME}': {ERROR}\",\n               \"NAME\", sensorName, \"ERROR\", e.what());\n    continue;\n}\n```\n\nInvalid configurations are now logged with detailed error messages, but the service continues to run. Other correctly configured sensors will start normally.\n\n**Verified on device**: Service continues running even with invalid units:\n```\nNov 24 02:34:28 bmc externalsensor[1141]: Invalid units for sensor: xyz.openbmc_project.Sensor.Value.Unit.DegreesC\nNov 24 02:34:28 bmc externalsensor[1141]: Failed to create ExternalSensor 'SWB_PCIe_Switch_Die_Temp_C': Invalid units for sensor\n```\n\nThe service does not crash."
                }
            ],
